// Everything Switchboard can do, for Jarvis (lib/jarvisapi.js finds and runs these).
// One entry per API route: what it does in plain words, its inputs, and its kind:
//   read     only looks
//   change   creates, edits, starts or connects something; easily undone
//   delete   removes, clears, signs out, merges, updates: Jarvis asks you first
//   send     reaches another person (mail, chat, a review, an invitation):
//            never Jarvis's to do; every send is your click (AGENTS.md)
//   internal plumbing only the page or a script uses
// test/jarvisapi.test.js fails when a route in lib/routes has no entry here, so a
// new feature cannot ship without Jarvis being able to use it.
